Cloud Computing with AWS (Amazon Web Services): 
Cloud computing is the delivery of computing services (servers, storage, databases, networking, software, and analytics) over the internet ("the cloud"). It allows users to access and store data remotely, reducing the need for local infrastructure while providing scalability, flexibility, and cost-efficiency. 
In this training, you will learn:

Cloud infrastructure basics
Cloud architecture principles
Various cloud services
How to deploy and manage infrastructure and applications in the cloud
 
The DevOps culture: 
DevOps is a collaborative approach that combines software development (Dev) and IT Operations(Ops) practices to facilitate and make the software development and deployment process more reliable. It focuses on teamwork, automation, and continuous improvement to quickly build, test, and release software. 
In this training, you will master:

DevOps tools and best practices
Version control (Git)
Continuous Integration/Continuous Deployment (CI/CD)
Configuration management
Containerization and orchestration
Infrastructure as Code (IaC)
Monitoring and logging
Security (DevSecOps) and more
 

